Build option MESEN_VIRTUAL_CLOCK: the cartridges' real-time clocks read a
time of day the host gives, not the host's own clock.

Three clocks in Mesen read the host's time: the Game Boy's MBC3 clock (when
a saved game with its clock is loaded, to run it forward by the time the
game was off), the SPC7110's RTC-4513 (Super Famicom) and the S-3511A of
the Game Boy Advance and WonderSwan cartridges (each time the game reads
it). A machine that reads the host's clock is another machine in every
run. With this option they read MesenVirtualClockMs, milliseconds since
1970-01-01 UTC, which the host sets from a setting and moves forward with
the machine's own time. Off, nothing changes.

